WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.309 --> 00:00:02.119
(upbeat violin music)

00:00:02.119 --> 00:00:04.829
- You lose your sight, and
everything gets a little harder.

00:00:04.829 --> 00:00:06.179
Everything takes longer.

00:00:06.179 --> 00:00:08.517
The walls seem to be caving
in on you all the time.

00:00:08.517 --> 00:00:10.909
When I was introduced to blind sailing,

00:00:10.909 --> 00:00:13.320
it was really an opportunity
for me to push the walls out,

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.657
to feel reconnected with the earth.

00:00:16.657 --> 00:00:19.824
(upbeat violin music)

00:00:22.799 --> 00:00:25.811
(upbeat harp music)

00:00:25.811 --> 00:00:26.749
My name's Walt Raineri.

00:00:26.749 --> 00:00:31.080
I'm the skipper of Blind
Match Racing Team USA 1,

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.200
for the Blind Match
Racing World Championships

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.339
here in Sheboygan, Wisconsin.

00:00:35.339 --> 00:00:38.097
For myself as a visually
impaired individual

00:00:38.097 --> 00:00:39.439
I'm looking forward to putting

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:40.659
a lot of this stuff
I've been thinking about

00:00:40.659 --> 00:00:43.051
for the last couple of
months into practice.

00:00:43.051 --> 00:00:44.600
You hold in and I'll kick off.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.433
Tell me when.

00:00:45.433 --> 00:00:47.800
- When we're racing, there's
no sighted people on the boat.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.699
It's just the three blind crew members.

00:00:50.699 --> 00:00:54.449
- You're relying on
other members of the crew

00:00:55.451 --> 00:00:57.000
literally for your life.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.408
It doesn't take long for
that bond to develop.

00:01:00.408 --> 00:01:02.120
- This is the blue one right here,

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.171
so I push the blue fob button.

00:01:04.171 --> 00:01:06.440
(blaring alarm)

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.600
(upbeat music)

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.920
- There's three buoys
in blind match racing.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.651
Each of those buoys
makes a distinct sound.

00:01:15.651 --> 00:01:18.240
- We listen for where the
buoys are on the water

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.489
and we navigate using
mental triangulation.

00:01:22.489 --> 00:01:26.131
By basis of where we are
in relation to those buoys,

00:01:26.131 --> 00:01:29.440
we know where we are in the water.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:30.539
There are many times when the boats are

00:01:30.539 --> 00:01:32.229
coming right at one another,

00:01:32.229 --> 00:01:33.451
and we need to know where they are,

00:01:33.451 --> 00:01:34.579
they need to know where we are.

00:01:34.579 --> 00:01:36.320
(whistle)

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.259
Each of the boats has a sound emitter.

00:01:39.259 --> 00:01:42.478
Vision is, by far, a human
being's predominant sense.

00:01:42.478 --> 00:01:43.640
But you take away the vision,

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.448
the audio sense picks up real quick.

00:01:45.448 --> 00:01:47.477
(beeping) There you go.

00:01:47.477 --> 00:01:49.877
Pressure's feeling better now.

00:01:49.877 --> 00:01:52.819
At times it feels like a
little bit of controlled chaos.

00:01:52.819 --> 00:01:54.259
- Where are they, where are they?

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:56.357
- The truth of it is, with a good team,

00:01:56.357 --> 00:01:57.440
and jibe ho,

00:02:00.272 --> 00:02:02.979
everything is under control,

00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:04.957
as chaotic as it may look.

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:08.259
(upbeat music)

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:11.579
About 12 years ago now, just about,

00:02:11.579 --> 00:02:15.857
I lost 95% of my vision in about 5 months.

00:02:15.857 --> 00:02:17.712
I had a very, very tough period of time,

00:02:17.712 --> 00:02:20.966
until one day I figured
out how to stop being

00:02:20.966 --> 00:02:23.397
a poorly functioning sighted person

00:02:23.397 --> 00:02:27.167
and start being a highly
functioning blind person,

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:29.197
and then began doing
things that I'd never done

00:02:29.197 --> 00:02:31.899
before I lost my sight, including sailing.

00:02:31.899 --> 00:02:33.797
For anyone who thinks that
they can't do something,

00:02:33.797 --> 00:02:35.597
it's too hard, it's too complicated,

00:02:35.597 --> 00:02:37.459
it's too frustrating, I'm here to tell you

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:39.128
that's just not true.

00:02:39.128 --> 00:02:40.947
Add a little courage, and you can do

00:02:40.947 --> 00:02:42.176
just about anything.

00:02:42.176 --> 00:02:44.759
(upbeat music)

